keywords:
  - xenium
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - image-registration
  - H&E
  - VALIS
  - HEST
abstract: >-
  hexenium is an installable pipeline for registering H&E
  whole-slide images against the DAPI morphology channel of a
  matched 10x Xenium in-situ transcriptomics run. It wraps VALIS
  (via valis_hest) and HEST into a single CLI (`hexenium run …`)
  with a resumable stage graph (he_preprocess → register → warp →
  celltype → viz) and a YAML-driven config surface.
